title: vossCopy2startDay1
---
<<jump test3>>
<<jump test2>>
This is an example/Reference of how to set up dialog

The first node of Dialog MUST be named in this manner
The Starting Node set in the NPCData scriptable object attached
to the npcInteract
AND 'startDay1' or 'startDay2/3/4' depending on what day this dialog is for

! its best to keep all dialog for a character across days on one big YS script,
and break it up into different days instead of multiple scripts

How to check if player has an item?

You can check if the player has obtained evidence that has either been
SCANNED or NOT SCANNED using this command. 

<<if HasItem("objectID")>>
if the player has that object then anything written here
will be run 

! the objectID is the OBJECT HOLDERS NAME 
^ the inspectable object that has the interactableObj script 
NOT ITS CHILD 
<<endif>>

! if you want to check if the player has an item that 
WAS SCANNED. then you run this command a little differently.
<<if HasItem("objectID_scan")>>

! this will be the same objectID but with _scan 
^^^ do not edit the gameobject's name to include _scan,
the scripts will automatically add it to inventory with that 

<<endif>>

<<jump testNode>>
===
title: testNode
---
This node tests if the player has inspected the object 
<<if HasItem("ObjHolder")>>

The player has the item ObjHolder

<<endif>>

<<if HasItem("ObjHolder_scan")>>

The player has the item ObjHolder AND has scanned it

<<endif>>


This checks for the players SANITY LEVEL 
// The value of CheckSanity(x) x should always just be 0 (it doesn't matter)
// and then use any operator (just like a regular if statement)
// == >= <= !=

<<if CheckSanity(0) == 5>>
    player sanity is equal to 5
<<endif>>


This updates the players evidence board, allowing the player to see an 
image of the NPC, their basic description, AND scan information 

^ you can set what these are on their npcData scriptable object. 

This function takes an arguement of the NPC's GAMEOBJECT NAME. make sure the string
EXACTLY MATCHES the name of their gameobject 

<<AddNPC "Tester">>

^ you should call this function ONCE throughout the entirety of the game. 
prefrably the first time you talk to them. 
:D
===
title: test2
---
This lets you show a notification :)
<<Notify "Hello :D">>
The notification plays right after the command! and doesn't only play at the end of dialog


This lets you change the players sanity.
IF you want to increase sanity, it should be a positive integer. and if you want to decrease it should
be a negative integer. (1 or -1) 
! keep in mind that sanity goes from 0-5, 0 being the lowest (bad) 
<<UpdateSanity -1>>

This is a check if the player has entered a certain room.
Currently this only checks for Bedroom

Don't change the string "Bedroom", but you can change the boolean to false if you need

<<if CheckEnter("Bedroom") == true>>
    The player has entered the bedroom.
    Here you would have the npc's node jump to the dialog they'd have if you 
    entered the bedroom
<<endif>>

<<if CheckEnter("Bedroom") == false>>
    The player has NOT entered the bedroom.
    Here you would have the npc's node jump to the dialog they'd have if you 
    entered the bedroom
<<endif>>

===
title: testInfoNode
---
you can call the node whatever you want, 
this would be what plays when the player chooses the info option 
when interacting with an npc 

you can set which node plays by editing the InitalConvoNode on their NPCInteract script in the inspector :)

